%% The single-field update composer: one box a person types or dictates into.
%% Both buttons always produce something, with or without a backend.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant P as Person
  participant UI as Composer (browser)
  participant API as POST /api/agent/summarize
  participant SA as Server agent
  participant M as Model provider

  P->>UI: one free-text note (typed or dictated)
  P->>UI: press "Clean up" or "Summarize"
  UI->>API: itemId, mode, raw text, the agent seed
  alt a backend is present and a model is configured
    API->>SA: validated body
    SA->>M: cleanup, or summarize with the recent thread
    alt the model answers
      M-->>SA: text, proposedStatus, questions
      SA->>SA: drop a status outside the allowed set and cap the questions
      SA-->>UI: source is llm, with the provider and model named
    else the model errors or returns nothing
      SA-->>UI: source is rules (deterministic cleanup)
    end
  else no backend (static export) or the request fails
    UI->>UI: local cleanup in the browser
    Note over UI: source is rules-local, so the copy never claims a model ran
  end
  UI-->>P: the proposed update, fully editable
  P->>UI: confirm and post
  UI->>API: POST /api/events with update.posted
  Note over P,API: the model never posts anything. A person confirms every word
